05:47.190 --> 05:48.210
A diary?

05:49.780 --> 05:56.660
I only have a few more years to
live. Having come to terms with that,
I write this in order to live together
with my disease. First off,
the pancreas disease I have is...

05:52.100 --> 05:53.320
Pancreas...

05:54.440 --> 05:55.370
Die?

05:56.020 --> 05:58.380
That's mine.

06:05.510 --> 06:06.550
Bet you're surprised.

06:06.960 --> 06:10.060
But not as surprised as I was!

06:10.060 --> 06:15.260
I thought I'd lost that thing and ran around everywhere looking, only to find you holding it!

06:15.260 --> 06:16.810
Oh, is that so?

06:16.810 --> 06:20.560
The people with the below ticket numbers, please wait a little longer.

06:16.810 --> 06:20.560
Billing

06:16.810 --> 06:20.560
If you are feeling ill, please inform a staff member.         Wait time is roughly 20 minutes.           If you are feeling ill, please inform a staff member.

06:16.810 --> 06:20.560
When your number is shown, please come to counter A2.

06:18.080 --> 06:23.290
Ticket number 54, please come to counter A2.

06:21.940 --> 06:22.810
Here you go.

06:23.290 --> 06:24.770
I repeat.

06:24.770 --> 06:29.830
Ticket number 54, please come to counter A2.

06:29.830 --> 06:31.070
You read it, right?

06:34.090 --> 06:36.360
I call it "Living with Dying."

06:36.360 --> 06:40.670
Ever since I learned about my pancreas disease, I've used it like a diary.

06:42.650 --> 06:44.710
You don't think I'm joking, do you?

06:45.160 --> 06:47.780
My sense of humor's not that dark!

06:54.290 --> 06:57.310
My pancreas has stopped working,

06:58.360 --> 06:59.980
and soon...

07:03.690 --> 07:05.150
I will die.

07:09.730 --> 07:10.780
You don't say.

07:12.780 --> 07:13.950
What?!

07:13.950 --> 07:15.240
That's it?!

07:15.240 --> 07:17.130
Were you listening to me?!

07:17.130 --> 07:22.800
Normally you'd act more surprised or say something poetic like "the fairest flowers soonest fade" to cheer me up.

07:22.800 --> 07:25.210
Don't you have anything else to say?

07:29.960 --> 07:30.840
No.

07:36.220 --> 07:37.480
Are you serious?

07:40.100 --> 07:41.730
Sorry, sorry.

07:42.190 --> 07:43.830
Anyway, I have to go to the counter.

07:59.330 --> 08:01.000
What a coincidence!

08:02.460 --> 08:05.270
Sorry, but don't drag me into your coincidences.

08:16.050 --> 08:19.930
Hey, have we ever even talked before?

08:20.360 --> 08:22.440
You've always got your nose in a book.

08:23.740 --> 08:25.320
Why were you at the hospital?

08:25.320 --> 08:25.940
A cold?

08:26.410 --> 08:28.690
It does seem to be going around.

08:30.430 --> 08:32.320
I'll be late to the trolley.

08:32.320 --> 08:33.090
See you.

08:36.340 --> 08:37.600
Okay, I get it.

08:37.600 --> 08:38.910
Just hold up a second.

08:38.910 --> 08:40.830
Let me ask a favor before you run off.

08:41.460 --> 08:45.090
I want you to keep my illness a secret.

08:45.090 --> 08:47.080
I haven't told anyone.

08:47.400 --> 08:49.540
It'll be our own little secret.

08:51.230 --> 08:52.210
I won't tell anyone.

08:52.850 --> 08:54.590
It's not like I have anyone to tell.

08:55.040 --> 08:56.590
You don't have any friends?

08:56.980 --> 09:00.600
If you want, I'll spend the rest of my life hanging out with you.

09:01.410 --> 09:03.090
I'm good.

09:03.090 --> 09:05.480
You should live however you want.

09:06.920 --> 09:08.030
Will do!

09:12.820 --> 09:14.220
Thanks!

09:15.040 --> 09:18.280
I thought we'd never have anything to do with each other again.

09:19.490 --> 09:20.790
But the following week,

09:20.790 --> 09:25.020
she volunteered for a vacant library assistant position, for whatever reason.

09:27.330 --> 09:29.840
Man, that was heavy.

09:29.840 --> 09:32.140
Do we have to do this every day?

09:32.140 --> 09:33.150
Yes.

09:33.150 --> 09:34.380
What?

09:34.920 --> 09:37.250
This is an important part of the job.

09:38.010 --> 09:39.650
Why did you sign up for this?

09:41.000 --> 09:42.220
Who knows.

09:42.710 --> 09:44.690
Do you even like books?

09:44.690 --> 09:46.120
Not at all.

09:46.120 --> 09:48.270
Oh, I do read a lot of comics!

09:49.840 --> 09:51.240
Hey, tell me.

09:51.240 --> 09:54.820
Do you really want to spend the rest of your short life in a library?

09:55.300 --> 09:57.280
Obviously. Why wouldn't I?

09:57.930 --> 10:00.090
I'm not sure what's "obvious" about it.

10:00.090 --> 10:02.370
What else should I be doing, then?

10:04.110 --> 10:06.600
Maybe meeting up with your first crush

10:06.600 --> 10:10.360
or hitchhiking in a foreign country and finding a nice place to die, or something.

10:11.620 --> 10:14.930
I get where you're coming from...

10:14.930 --> 10:18.900
But don't you have things you want to do before dying too?

10:21.390 --> 10:22.890
I suppose I do.

10:22.890 --> 10:25.840
Yet you're not doing them right now.

10:25.840 --> 10:28.640
Even though you never know if you'll drop dead tomorrow!

10:29.700 --> 10:33.900
That's true for me and just as much for you.

10:35.980 --> 10:38.920
Every day is worth the same as any other.

10:38.920 --> 10:42.300
What I did or didn't do today doesn't change its worth.

10:42.980 --> 10:47.580
I have fun doing normal stuff just like this!

10:49.620 --> 10:50.680
You don't say.

10:51.320 --> 10:53.200
Oh, that's right.

10:53.750 --> 10:57.970
I'm making a list of things I want to do before dying in this book,

10:57.970 --> 11:01.220
and I'll do you the favor of letting you come along!

11:01.850 --> 11:04.060
Where is this coming from?

11:04.060 --> 11:06.420
You're contradicting what you just said.

11:06.420 --> 11:08.360
Are you free after this?

11:08.360 --> 11:11.150
You can't be very busy with no friends, right?

11:11.680 --> 11:14.000
Thanks, but I'm good.

11:15.300 --> 11:16.360
Oh?

11:16.360 --> 11:20.200
Weren't you the one who told me to live however I want?

11:20.740 --> 11:21.530
What?

11:21.530 --> 11:23.200
Oh, that's not what I—

11:23.490 --> 11:26.160
Well, I want to drag you along!

11:28.960 --> 11:30.890
That's so good!

11:30.890 --> 11:33.130
Just go with your family for yakiniku.

11:33.130 --> 11:36.820
Don't be like that. Here, eat more offal.

11:36.820 --> 11:37.790
Hey!

11:41.310 --> 11:43.370
That's sweetbread. You know, the pancreas.

11:47.960 --> 11:52.390
Don't tell me eating cow entrails is also part of your treatment?

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Yen

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
90 minutes

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
All you can eat! !

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
ice cream

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Yakiniku / Offal

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Now you can eat meat for lunch during the week!

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Including tax

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
+1,000 yen for all you can drink!

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Rice, soup, salad,

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
pickled vegetables,

11:52.390 --> 12:04.660
Lunch time

11:53.420 --> 11:55.090
No, I just like offal.

11:55.090 --> 11:58.290
If someone asked me my favorite food, I'd reply offal.

11:58.290 --> 12:00.090
Top of the list: entrails!

12:00.650 --> 12:03.360
Excuse me! More tripe and heart please!

12:03.360 --> 12:04.200
Coming up!

12:05.210 --> 12:07.010
Don't you have any dietary restrictions?

12:07.010 --> 12:08.620
No, not really.

12:09.200 --> 12:13.920
But that's apparently because there's been some nifty medical advancements in the last ten years or so.

12:14.700 --> 12:16.970
It's amazing what humans can do.

12:17.980 --> 12:22.260
Even though I'm sick, it doesn't get in the way of my life at all!

12:22.260 --> 12:23.950
Here you go, tripe and heart.

12:26.210 --> 12:28.680
You know, I don't want to be cremated.

12:30.260 --> 12:32.980
Is that something to talk about when we're grilling meat?

12:33.380 --> 12:36.150
You can eat my pancreas if you want.

12:36.150 --> 12:37.120
Did you hear me?

12:39.360 --> 12:41.270
I looked it up after we talked,

12:41.270 --> 12:48.500
and apparently there's a foreign religion where if someone else eats you, your soul will live on inside of them.

12:48.500 --> 12:49.680
No thanks.

12:49.680 --> 12:52.020
Your soul would just be a constant racket.

12:53.650 --> 12:54.920
I bet.

12:55.610 --> 12:56.690
By the way,

12:56.690 --> 12:59.440
is there no one in our class you're close to?

12:59.440 --> 13:03.510
I realized I don't know a thing about you.

13:05.130 --> 13:08.450
Everyone thinks of me as just a boring classmate,

13:08.450 --> 13:10.280
or even worse.

13:10.860 --> 13:13.120
Have people actually told you that?

13:13.930 --> 13:15.170
No, they haven't.

13:15.170 --> 13:16.650
But that's what I think.

13:16.650 --> 13:18.910
You can't know that.

13:18.910 --> 13:20.600
It's all in your head.

13:20.600 --> 13:22.860
There's no telling if you're right.

13:23.650 --> 13:25.890
It doesn't matter if I'm right or not.

13:26.440 --> 13:28.310
It's just what I believe.

13:29.140 --> 13:34.500
It's my hobby to imagine what someone thinks about me.

13:36.610 --> 13:40.000
Then, how do you think I think of you?

13:41.160 --> 13:42.230
The same.

13:42.230 --> 13:47.260
Boring Classmate, or perhaps
Classmate Who Knows My Secret.

13:51.480 --> 13:53.390
Hmm, maybe so?

13:54.640 --> 13:57.810
Like I said, it doesn't really matter either way for me.

13:58.400 --> 14:01.760
But where'd you come up with that thought process in the first place?

14:03.890 --> 14:05.650
He is rich that has few wants.

14:07.240 --> 14:08.030
What's that mean?

14:09.450 --> 14:14.990
Excepting my family, I'm happy to let all my personal relationships begin and end in my head.

14:16.000 --> 14:18.890
Someone liking or disliking me is all my imagination.

14:20.400 --> 14:22.740
As long as there's no harm to me,

14:22.740 --> 14:24.760
it doesn't matter if they like me or hate me.

14:27.090 --> 14:29.920
So I don't have any interest in others.

14:31.050 --> 14:33.350
And others don't have any interest in me.

14:33.350 --> 14:35.100
Well, I'm interested!

14:35.570 --> 14:36.390
Huh?

14:36.770 --> 14:39.580
I wouldn't invite someone I'm not interested in!

14:40.720 --> 14:42.110
Don't treat me like an idiot!

14:48.460 --> 14:53.020
I think you do idiotic things every now and then,
but I'm not trying to treat you like one.

14:53.580 --> 14:56.430
Maybe that's what's in your head,

14:56.430 --> 14:59.040
but you're still making me mad!

14:59.040 --> 15:01.170
I can't eat all that!

15:03.980 --> 15:06.110
Nice weather today.

15:08.720 --> 15:11.000
Maybe I should die on a day like this.

15:11.730 --> 15:13.430
Are you still sulking?

15:13.770 --> 15:15.160
Not especially.

15:22.230 --> 15:23.980
Look at this mess.

15:24.680 --> 15:28.490
Lady, my clothes are all stained thanks to you.

15:28.790 --> 15:32.050
You'll pay to have them cleaned, won'tcha?

15:32.050 --> 15:35.030
Y-You're the ones who ran into her with your bikes—

15:35.030 --> 15:39.080
'Scuse me? This hag was standing in the middle of the goddamn road!

15:39.080 --> 15:41.580
Are you saying you'll pay for her?

15:41.870 --> 15:43.180
What's going on?

15:42.520 --> 15:44.840
Hey! Say something!

15:43.180 --> 15:44.840
I'm not sure...

15:44.840 --> 15:46.160
Hey!

15:46.160 --> 15:48.330
Are you deaf?

15:48.330 --> 15:49.590
Let's go around.

15:48.880 --> 15:49.590
Hey!

15:52.970 --> 15:53.760
Huh?

15:53.760 --> 15:55.480
Hey! How'll it be?

15:55.480 --> 15:57.340
Cough up the dough already!

15:57.340 --> 15:59.040
You're the ones at fault here!

15:59.040 --> 15:59.840
Huh?

15:59.840 --> 16:01.330
Ma'am, are you all right?

16:01.330 --> 16:02.720
Couldn't you hear me?

16:02.720 --> 16:04.560
This is your fault, not hers!

16:04.560 --> 16:06.290
Who the hell are you?

16:06.290 --> 16:09.230
Bicycles aren't allowed on the shopping street, you know.

16:09.660 --> 16:11.380
Can't you read that sign?

16:12.090 --> 16:13.280
Apologize to her!

16:13.610 --> 16:15.360
You fucking brat!

16:15.360 --> 16:17.450
You looking for a world of hurt?!

16:17.450 --> 16:19.140
Oh, resorting to violence, are we?

16:17.900 --> 16:20.100
Hey, could you watch the store for a bit?

16:19.140 --> 16:21.290
With all these onlookers?

16:21.290 --> 16:24.210
It's pretty clear who'd be found guilty in court!

16:24.970 --> 16:25.920
You there!

16:25.920 --> 16:27.290
Stop it right there!

16:30.440 --> 16:32.670
This is for the old lady!

16:39.120 --> 16:40.200
Hey, what the fuck?!

16:40.200 --> 16:43.900
Oh, she got both of them good.

16:48.270 --> 16:49.080
Nice one!

16:49.080 --> 16:50.150
Ouch, that gotta hurt.

16:50.150 --> 16:51.670
Looking good, kid!

16:55.610 --> 16:57.290
See ya, lady!

16:57.290 --> 16:58.340
Hey, hold it!

16:58.340 --> 16:59.530
Stop it!

16:59.530 --> 17:01.660
You too! Wait up!

17:00.760 --> 17:01.660
Ow!

17:02.640 --> 17:03.610
Let's scram!

17:03.610 --> 17:05.080
H-Hey, wait!

17:12.640 --> 17:16.300
Why... did you have to go and... do something like that?

17:18.900 --> 17:20.260
That was scary.

17:20.890 --> 17:23.720
I feel like I might run out of breath ahead of schedule!

17:23.720 --> 17:28.810
I think this is the first time... I've heard that used... literally.

17:32.100 --> 17:33.410
Hey, look at this!

17:33.410 --> 17:36.760
This place's name is perfect for me!

17:36.760 --> 17:37.620
Huh?

17:37.620 --> 17:38.420
All right!

17:38.420 --> 17:39.540
We're going in here!

17:39.540 --> 17:41.880
Spring goes hand in hand with sakura—cherry blossoms.

17:42.540 --> 17:44.780
Are you talking about your name?

17:44.780 --> 17:47.220
I'm all thirsty from running. Let's go in.

18:01.560 --> 18:03.980
This is a nice place we came across.

18:06.070 --> 18:06.880
Hey.

18:08.510 --> 18:11.530
Do you know why cherry blossoms bloom in spring?

18:13.980 --> 18:19.620
Once the blossoms have fallen in April, it actually just takes three months for them to sprout buds again.

18:20.300 --> 18:22.640
They wait almost a year for it to become warm

18:22.640 --> 18:24.490
and then bloom all at once.

18:26.170 --> 18:28.990
Sakura are waiting for the right time to bloom.

18:30.590 --> 18:31.740
Isn't that wonderful?

18:40.600 --> 18:43.570
I'm gonna tell Kyoko about this place.

18:44.660 --> 18:48.000
Oh, the three of us should totally come here sometime!

18:48.000 --> 18:49.960
Hey, give me your contact info!

18:49.960 --> 18:50.970
No thanks.

18:51.750 --> 18:54.060
Come on, give me your phone.

18:54.060 --> 18:56.530
It's just for the short while until I die.

18:56.530 --> 18:59.720
We have to make sure to keep close contact.

19:01.970 --> 19:05.220
The female stabbing victim has been confirmed dead.

19:03.920 --> 19:05.410
I'm home.

19:05.410 --> 19:06.510
Welcome back.

19:06.510 --> 19:07.680
Are you having dinner?

19:07.680 --> 19:08.680
Not hungry.

19:10.910 --> 19:13.320
Coming up is the weather.

19:13.320 --> 19:14.500
Tomorrow, all of Japan—

19:16.310 --> 19:17.590
Thanks for today!

19:17.590 --> 19:20.030
Thanks for going along with me.

19:20.030 --> 19:21.990
I had a lot of fun!

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
See you!

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
I hope we can get along well

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
Inbox

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
Sakura Yamauchi

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
No subject

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
until I die!

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
I had a lot of fun!

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
Thanks for going along with me

19:20.720 --> 19:23.510
Thanks for today!

19:21.990 --> 19:23.510
I hope we can get along until I die!

19:24.440 --> 19:25.480
See you!

19:27.960 --> 19:29.900
Oh no, there he is.

19:32.470 --> 19:33.890
So did you hear about it?

19:36.160 --> 19:37.690
Morning, everyone.

19:37.690 --> 19:40.490
Sakura! What's your relationship with that guy?

19:47.850 --> 19:50.120
Hey, so are you close to Yamauchi or what?

19:50.770 --> 19:53.710
Apparently people saw you two together yesterday.

19:54.210 --> 19:55.520
Not really.

19:55.520 --> 19:57.040
I just happened to run into her.

19:58.590 --> 20:00.030
I see...

20:03.920 --> 20:04.800
Want some gum?

20:05.160 --> 20:07.670
Thanks, but I'm good.

20:07.670 --> 20:08.410
Aight.

20:08.850 --> 20:12.350
Well, lemme know if anything interesting happens.

20:12.350 --> 20:15.790
Right? There are plenty of better guys we could introduce you to!

20:15.790 --> 20:19.410
Yeah! You're way out of his league!

20:19.410 --> 20:22.490
It's not like that. We just get along.

20:22.490 --> 20:24.300
What's that supposed to mean?

20:24.300 --> 20:25.140
Good morning.

20:25.990 --> 20:27.280
Good morning!

20:27.280 --> 20:28.050
Morning!

20:28.050 --> 20:29.170
Hey!

20:28.340 --> 20:29.170
Good morning.

20:30.320 --> 20:31.000
Sakura!

20:31.360 --> 20:35.100
I found a CD by the band you were talking about a the store near the station.

20:35.100 --> 20:38.140
Wow! It's that super rare one that went out of print!

20:38.140 --> 20:40.130
I already listened to it, so I'll lend it to you.

20:40.130 --> 20:41.290
Thank you!

20:41.290 --> 20:41.990
Sure.

20:43.970 --> 20:44.760
Yo!

20:44.760 --> 20:46.210
Takahiro!

20:45.020 --> 20:46.000
Good morning.

20:46.210 --> 20:48.000
Let me copy your homework!

20:48.000 --> 20:49.570
Did you forget to do it again?

20:48.970 --> 20:51.600
Takahiro would be way better boyfriend material!

20:51.600 --> 20:53.850
Great at sports, and has both looks and smarts.

20:53.850 --> 20:55.940
He's our hottie class rep!

20:56.360 --> 20:58.970
I'm telling you, it's not like that.

20:58.970 --> 21:02.020
You've got the looks to be picky, so don't settle for that.

21:02.020 --> 21:02.940
You know it!

21:03.540 --> 21:06.320
Come on, don't be so mean!

21:06.800 --> 21:08.670
It's such a shame!

21:14.370 --> 21:18.290
Hey, I have another place on my bucket list I want to visit today.

21:18.960 --> 21:19.900
Okay.

21:19.900 --> 21:21.520
But I'll pass.

21:21.980 --> 21:24.470
I'd rather not have everyone ridicule me again.

21:24.840 --> 21:27.290
Wait, that reminds me!

21:27.290 --> 21:31.360
You told the people in class that we're not close, didn't you?

21:31.360 --> 21:32.680
Yeah. What about it?

21:32.980 --> 21:34.330
I told you in my text!

21:34.330 --> 21:36.060
For us to get along until I die.

21:36.900 --> 21:39.850
I'm fine with people observing me,

21:39.850 --> 21:43.320
but I don't want them talking to me or prying into my life.

21:45.990 --> 21:50.080
Wanting to keep your secret is part of it,
you know. You should be thanking me.

21:50.490 --> 21:52.240
I don't see why you should be angry with me.

21:54.080 --> 21:58.160
With this and your taste in meat, we're totally not aligned!

21:58.160 --> 21:59.580
You may be right.

21:59.580 --> 22:01.250
We're complete opposites.

22:05.510 --> 22:06.580
Yeah, that's it!

22:06.580 --> 22:07.720
Complete opposites!

22:08.830 --> 22:10.170
Keep it down.

22:10.170 --> 22:11.260
We're in a library.

22:11.660 --> 22:12.510
Oops.

22:13.910 --> 22:16.810
To go back to what I was saying, you'll come along, right?

22:16.810 --> 22:17.640
Where to?

22:19.510 --> 22:20.710
Paradise!

22:23.420 --> 22:26.360
They have really good shortcake here.

22:26.890 --> 22:30.460
You should be going here with your girlfriends.

22:34.650 --> 22:37.140
Listen, are you trying to get fat?

22:37.700 --> 22:39.500
Or are you trying to make me fat?

22:40.170 --> 22:42.050
You're only bringing me to all-you-can-eats.

22:42.050 --> 22:43.930
It's neither!

22:43.930 --> 22:46.380
I just want to eat what I want to eat.

22:48.740 --> 22:51.580
Hey, are you interested in girls at all?

22:51.580 --> 22:53.140
Where is this coming from?

22:53.420 --> 22:56.640
You're not even batting an eye at all the cuties here.

22:56.640 --> 22:58.180
Have you even had a girlfriend?

22:59.100 --> 23:00.360
Of course not.

23:00.890 --> 23:02.850
I've never even had a friend.

23:03.290 --> 23:04.680
Never?

23:04.680 --> 23:07.130
You've never wanted friends or a girlfriend?

23:09.450 --> 23:10.210
I wonder.

23:10.960 --> 23:14.420
It might have been fun to have a friend or two,

23:15.040 --> 23:19.770
but I believe that the world of fiction is more fun than reality.

23:20.690 --> 23:23.260
That explains why you're always reading.

23:24.480 --> 23:25.710
You know, I...

23:27.340 --> 23:29.570
...broke up with my boyfriend recently.

23:30.580 --> 23:32.570
Because you'll die soon?

23:32.570 --> 23:33.860
No, no.

23:33.860 --> 23:36.490
I'd never tell my boyfriend that.

23:36.490 --> 23:38.760
Oh, it's someone you know, by the way.

23:38.760 --> 23:40.400
He's in our class.

23:40.940 --> 23:43.550
But I guess you wouldn't know his name anyway.

23:45.360 --> 23:49.400
You see, he's a great person to have as a friend,

23:49.400 --> 23:52.050
but he didn't really work out as a boyfriend.

23:52.580 --> 23:54.820
He's overly persistent in ways.

23:55.990 --> 23:57.690
Kyoko!

23:57.690 --> 23:58.840
What?

23:58.840 --> 23:59.650
Look.

24:01.920 --> 24:03.050
We really ate a lot.

24:03.050 --> 24:04.090
Yeah.

24:05.400 --> 24:06.560
Sakura!

24:08.990 --> 24:10.760
Kyoko, you're here too?

24:12.090 --> 24:14.120
This is my best friend, Kyoko.

24:17.920 --> 24:20.820
Sakura, are you seriously on good terms with this guy?

24:20.820 --> 24:22.890
Yeah, I just told you earlier today.

24:27.130 --> 24:31.010
Listen, Sakura, it's not that I want to complain.

24:31.010 --> 24:34.290
But, like... You've been alone together two days in a row!

24:36.090 --> 24:37.460
Are you dating?

24:37.460 --> 24:38.200
Nope.

24:38.630 --> 24:40.120
Then what?!

24:40.120 --> 24:42.710
I told you, we're just getting along.

24:42.710 --> 24:44.040
What?!

24:44.040 --> 24:45.790
What's that even supposed to mean?!

24:46.190 --> 24:48.290
Kyoko! We're heading out!

24:49.690 --> 24:51.170
Shouldn't you be joining them?

24:54.380 --> 24:56.750
I'll make you spit it out tomorrow, okay?

24:59.420 --> 25:00.170
Sorry.

25:00.170 --> 25:01.320
How much was it?

25:00.470 --> 25:04.220
Man, I didn't expect Kyoko to be here.

25:04.220 --> 25:07.140
Kyoko's been my best friend since junior high.

25:07.960 --> 25:10.930
As you can see, she's pretty strong-willed,

25:10.930 --> 25:16.570
so at first I thought she was kinda scary, but once we started talking we became friends right away.

25:17.050 --> 25:19.810
She's a nice girl, so try and get along with her.

25:27.750 --> 25:30.840
Shouldn't you tell that best friend about your disease?

25:31.330 --> 25:32.960
Nah, it's fine.

25:32.960 --> 25:35.480
She gets pretty emotional, you know.

25:35.480 --> 25:38.450
She'd probably cry every time she saw me if I told her.

25:39.000 --> 25:41.040
That wouldn't be very fun, would it?

26:09.820 --> 26:10.840
Are you...

26:17.290 --> 26:18.660
Are you

26:18.660 --> 26:20.010
really dying?

26:23.580 --> 26:24.570
Sure am.

26:31.360 --> 26:35.030
You're the only one I can talk about this with.

26:36.850 --> 26:39.580
You're probably the only one

26:40.640 --> 26:46.040
who can give me reality and normalcy.

26:48.600 --> 26:53.100
The doctors can only offer me reality.

26:55.290 --> 27:03.900
My family overreacts to everything I say,
and they're desperately trying to pretend everything's normal.

27:05.810 --> 27:10.960
If Kyoko and the others found out, they'd probably act similarly distant.

27:13.390 --> 27:17.710
You're the only one who'll spend normal everyday life with me

27:17.710 --> 27:20.060
while still knowing what the reality is.

27:23.120 --> 27:24.130
So...

27:24.650 --> 27:26.210
Hanging out with you

27:26.680 --> 27:27.880
is fun!

27:38.430 --> 27:40.340
Hot weather has its own charm.

27:40.930 --> 27:44.130
Gotta enjoy it to the fullest.
It might be my last summer, after all.

27:44.970 --> 27:45.860
Thanks.

27:46.520 --> 27:51.540
Summer's all about the usual things:
the sea, fireworks, and festivals.

27:52.160 --> 27:54.860
Also, a fleeting summer rendezvous.

27:54.860 --> 27:56.590
A fleeting summer love...

27:56.590 --> 27:58.110
A youthful summer mistake.

27:58.760 --> 28:00.750
Now that I'm in high school,

28:00.750 --> 28:04.370
I should seize the chance to have one or two of those.

28:05.060 --> 28:06.800
So in other words,

28:06.800 --> 28:09.930
you still want to get a boyfriend?

28:15.170 --> 28:16.000
What's wrong?

28:17.960 --> 28:21.970
If I said I wanted a boyfriend, would you do something about it?

28:30.890 --> 28:31.980
What do you mean?

28:36.320 --> 28:37.190
Nothing.

28:37.960 --> 28:39.720
I didn't mean anything in particular.

28:41.280 --> 28:45.620
You're gravely mistaken if you think there's a purpose to everything I say!

28:49.320 --> 28:53.250
Instead of reading books all the time,
spend more time with people!

29:01.100 --> 29:01.970
Hey, Sakura.

29:01.970 --> 29:02.370
Hm?

29:02.370 --> 29:03.660
Wanna go out for karaoke?

29:03.660 --> 29:05.390
Nice idea, I'm in!

29:07.240 --> 29:08.640
Want some gum?

29:10.770 --> 29:11.940
No thanks.

29:12.540 --> 29:15.890
Dude, are you sure you and Sakura aren't dating?

29:15.890 --> 29:16.940
We're not.

29:16.940 --> 29:19.300
But you seem so close recently.

29:19.300 --> 29:20.280
Something happen?

29:24.340 --> 29:25.530
Wait, hold on!

29:26.050 --> 29:29.460
Don't tell me you think I'm asking you because I like Yamauchi!

29:29.460 --> 29:30.390
That's way off.

29:30.390 --> 29:32.950
See, I'm into more refined girls.

29:32.950 --> 29:34.490
Stop slacking off.

29:35.960 --> 29:38.740
I wasn't slacking off!

29:38.740 --> 29:41.220
I-I just thought I'd give him some gum.

29:41.220 --> 29:42.800
So you really were slacking off.

29:43.490 --> 29:45.400
Go and throw this away.

29:45.400 --> 29:47.060
Yeah, sure, no problem.

29:50.020 --> 29:53.060
I didn't kick you that hard!

29:54.750 --> 29:56.730
Get your butt back to cleaning, too.

30:22.890 --> 30:23.930
Finally!

30:23.930 --> 30:25.800
The break starts tomorrow!

30:25.800 --> 30:28.780
To get straight to the point: Are you free?

30:28.780 --> 30:31.930
I want to go on a train trip over the break!

30:31.930 --> 30:34.160
Is there anyplace you'd like to visit?

30:34.160 --> 30:37.610
Let's just go someplace you want to visit before dying.

30:37.610 --> 30:40.510
All right, let's meet up at the station tomorrow morning!

30:40.510 --> 30:42.860
Don't you dare stand me up!

30:43.390 --> 30:44.310
Good morning.

30:45.180 --> 30:48.060
Huh? Is that all the luggage you brought?

30:48.060 --> 30:48.610
Yeah.

30:48.610 --> 30:50.040
What about a change of clothes?

30:50.660 --> 30:51.560
Clothes?

30:53.010 --> 30:56.890
Well, you can just buy something when we finally get there. I'm sure they'll have a UNIQLO.

30:56.890 --> 30:57.980
Finally get there...

30:57.980 --> 30:59.080
UNIQLO...

31:00.290 --> 31:04.000
Come on, stop being so gloomy. You should be having fun on a trip like this.

31:04.580 --> 31:07.760
I'd say this is more like a kidnapping than a trip.

31:08.360 --> 31:11.940
Actually, I'm amazed your parents let you even go on this trip.

31:11.940 --> 31:13.400
On an overnight one at that.

31:13.400 --> 31:15.840
I told them I was going with Kyoko.

31:15.840 --> 31:19.480
If I tell my parents I have something I want to do before dying,

31:19.480 --> 31:22.370
they'll usually tearfully agree,

31:22.370 --> 31:25.230
but a trip with a guy is probably a bridge too far.

31:27.140 --> 31:29.990
What about you? What excuse are you going with?

31:31.090 --> 31:33.230
In order to keep my parents from worrying,

31:33.230 --> 31:35.780
I'm lying to them about having friends.

31:35.780 --> 31:38.770
I'll call home saying I'm sleeping at a friend's house later.

31:39.290 --> 31:41.040
That's awful. And sad.

31:41.690 --> 31:43.920
Just call it making sure no one is hurt.

31:43.920 --> 31:46.580
Hey, so about your last name...

31:48.340 --> 31:49.840
Is this the right spelling?

31:51.120 --> 31:52.480
No issue there.

31:52.480 --> 31:53.330
Thanks.

31:54.080 --> 31:54.680
Hey...

31:55.580 --> 31:58.720
Could you not write my name down in that?

31:58.720 --> 31:59.560
Why not?

32:00.250 --> 32:06.650
I don't want your parents or friends to pry or criticize me after you're dead.

32:06.650 --> 32:09.440
It's my book, so I can do what I want with it.

32:10.400 --> 32:12.400
Oh yeah, what was your first name?

32:12.400 --> 32:14.820
If I tell you, you'll just write it in there, won't you?

32:14.820 --> 32:17.200
Who cares? Not like it'll kill you.

32:24.170 --> 32:25.080
All right, fine.

32:45.200 --> 32:47.100
We've made landfall!

32:48.640 --> 32:50.010
I can smell ramen!

32:50.010 --> 32:51.970
That's got to be your imagination.

32:51.970 --> 32:53.450
No, I'm sure of it!

32:53.450 --> 32:55.290
Is your nose even working?

32:55.290 --> 32:57.290
At least my brain is, unlike you.

32:57.290 --> 32:59.370
The only thing not working is my pancreas!

33:00.320 --> 33:02.710
You know, things have been pretty dangerous lately.

33:02.710 --> 33:04.050
That's true.

33:04.050 --> 33:06.630
There was that stabbing in the next prefecture over, for one.

33:06.630 --> 33:09.130
I heard a police officer mention on TV

33:09.130 --> 33:12.260
that apparently that's the hardest kind of bad guy to catch.

33:12.260 --> 33:15.340
Only the good die young, as they say.

33:15.340 --> 33:17.930
I don't think you're using that one right.

33:17.930 --> 33:21.140
I guess that also explains why you'll survive and I'll die.

33:21.880 --> 33:25.520
I just realized something. You can't trust a saying.

33:26.000 --> 33:27.050
I'll remember that.

33:33.970 --> 33:35.270
What?!

33:36.250 --> 33:37.700
I'm terribly sorry.

33:42.580 --> 33:43.540
In that case...

33:43.120 --> 33:43.540
Yes?

33:44.150 --> 33:44.930
Hey.

33:46.870 --> 33:47.420
What?

33:48.130 --> 33:49.530
So, the thing is...

33:52.260 --> 33:54.800
We ended up in the same room, but you don't mind,  right?

33:56.070 --> 33:56.680
Huh?

33:58.720 --> 34:01.140
Apparently there was some mistake in the booking,

34:01.140 --> 34:05.980
and since it was their fault, they gave us a way better room than what we paid for!

34:06.340 --> 34:09.420
I'm pretty nervous about sleeping in the same bed as you!

34:09.800 --> 34:10.860
Are you stupid?

34:10.860 --> 34:12.360
I'll be sleeping over here.

34:12.730 --> 34:13.620
What?

34:13.620 --> 34:15.540
Now that we've got this nice room,

34:15.540 --> 34:18.120
you have to experience the bed too!

34:18.120 --> 34:20.740
Fine, I'll have a quick lie-down later.

34:21.080 --> 34:21.920
You do that!

34:21.920 --> 34:24.940
In the meantime, I'll be taking a bath.

34:27.030 --> 34:28.970
No peeking, got it?

34:50.620 --> 34:51.440
Hey!

34:51.960 --> 34:55.220
Could you bring me the face wash from my bag?

35:16.030 --> 35:17.030
Thanks!

35:17.820 --> 35:20.080
By the way, I'm butt naked right now!

35:22.760 --> 35:24.290
Come on, say something!

35:24.290 --> 35:25.550
This is embarrassing!

35:49.290 --> 35:52.540
Don't you find it romantic to be looking at the night skyline like this?

35:52.980 --> 35:53.930
Oh, right.

35:53.930 --> 35:57.630
I bought some stuff to drink while you were in the bath.

35:58.210 --> 35:59.570
Here, this is yours.

36:00.900 --> 36:01.880
Thank you.

36:06.140 --> 36:07.010
Wait, is this...

36:08.220 --> 36:10.400
Oh, don't be so stuck up.

36:10.400 --> 36:13.340
We've got cards, so why don't we play something?

36:13.340 --> 36:15.300
It's sad playing cards with just the two of us.

36:15.300 --> 36:17.740
Well, since we're already drinking,

36:17.740 --> 36:19.780
why don't we play truth or dare?

36:20.240 --> 36:22.780
What's that supposed to be? Sounds philosophical.

36:22.780 --> 36:23.730
You don't know it?

36:23.730 --> 36:24.200
No.

36:24.200 --> 36:26.640
Okay, I'll explain as we go.

36:27.820 --> 36:30.420
First off, there are ten rounds.

36:30.420 --> 36:33.060
You're not allowed to quit partway.

36:33.060 --> 36:36.400
You choose whichever card you like,
and the one with the highest number wins.

36:36.400 --> 36:37.500
Got it?

36:37.500 --> 36:38.380
Yeah.

36:39.160 --> 36:40.380
All right!

36:40.760 --> 36:42.840
Okay, I win.

36:42.840 --> 36:47.420
I'll ask you "truth or dare," so start off by replying "truth."

36:47.940 --> 36:48.850
Truth.

36:49.240 --> 36:51.640
Okay, to start off...

36:51.640 --> 36:54.610
Who do you think the cutest girl in our class is?

36:55.170 --> 36:58.110
Why are you springing a question like that?

36:58.110 --> 36:59.860
It's all part of the game.

37:00.220 --> 37:02.860
If you don't want to answer, you can choose dare.

37:03.610 --> 37:07.000
But in that case I'll order you to do something,

37:07.000 --> 37:09.080
and you have to do what I say.

37:09.900 --> 37:12.860
By the way, if you choose dare,

37:12.860 --> 37:14.580
I won't go easy on you.

37:16.120 --> 37:18.400
Who came up with this game? Satan?

37:18.400 --> 37:21.490
Also, no asking me to do perverted stuff.

37:21.490 --> 37:22.620
Are you an idiot?

37:24.460 --> 37:26.990
So, what's your answer to my question?

37:30.010 --> 37:31.930
If I had to go with someone...

37:31.930 --> 37:33.810
I think that one girl is pretty.

37:34.260 --> 37:36.850
The one who's good at math.

37:36.850 --> 37:39.110
Oh, you mean Hina!

37:41.160 --> 37:43.860
That's the kind of girl you like?

37:45.810 --> 37:48.240
Okay, next round, next round.

37:48.700 --> 37:49.960
Yay!

37:49.960 --> 37:51.690
Truth or dare?

37:51.690 --> 37:52.700
Truth.

37:52.700 --> 37:54.100
Then what about me?

37:54.100 --> 37:56.540
Where would you rank me in our class?

38:04.090 --> 38:08.200
This is just among the people I can recall,

38:09.850 --> 38:10.890
but third, maybe?

38:11.460 --> 38:16.770
Huh... You've been looking at me thinking that I'm the third-cutest in class?

38:18.330 --> 38:21.360
Also, I know I'm the one who asked,

38:21.790 --> 38:23.730
but that's super embarrassing.

38:24.640 --> 38:26.730
You really are an idiot.

38:26.730 --> 38:30.200
But I didn't expect you to give a serious reply!

38:34.280 --> 38:36.340
That caught me off guard.

38:36.340 --> 38:37.720
You still want to do this?

38:37.720 --> 38:39.820
Yes, obviously!

38:39.820 --> 38:41.470
I'm not sure what's obvious about it.

38:42.090 --> 38:44.470
Then, truth or dare?

38:44.470 --> 38:45.260
Truth!

38:45.910 --> 38:47.760
This is pretty nerve-racking!

38:51.040 --> 38:53.390
What were you like when you were young?

38:53.720 --> 38:54.530
What?

38:54.530 --> 38:55.640
Is that it?

38:56.500 --> 39:01.900
I'm just curious how you turned out like you did.

39:02.300 --> 39:04.770
I thought you weren't interested in others?

39:05.410 --> 39:09.460
Besides, I was fully prepared to tell you my measurements.

39:09.460 --> 39:10.500
Shut up.

39:13.960 --> 39:15.800
When I was young, huh...

39:16.370 --> 39:19.040
People always told me to settle down.

39:19.760 --> 39:23.740
I'd get in fights with the biggest guy in the class.

39:24.690 --> 39:26.620
Basically, I was a problem child.

39:28.800 --> 39:30.990
What's the hobby you've kept up the longest?

39:30.990 --> 39:34.310
Well, I guess I've always liked movies.

39:34.310 --> 39:36.800
What do you think are your weak and strong points?

39:36.800 --> 39:40.550
My strong point is being able to get along with anyone,

39:40.550 --> 39:43.730
and I guess my weak point is being easily distracted.

39:43.730 --> 39:45.730
What's the happiest thing you've experienced?

39:46.430 --> 39:48.570
Getting to know you, maybe!

39:49.250 --> 39:51.490
What's the saddest thing you've experienced?

39:52.130 --> 39:55.610
Probably the dog I grew up with dying.

39:56.240 --> 39:58.620
Hey, is this some kind of interview?

39:59.420 --> 40:00.870
Seriously...

40:00.870 --> 40:04.480
All these uptight questions are boring.

40:04.990 --> 40:06.260
Two more rounds.

40:07.120 --> 40:08.350
Ten.

40:08.350 --> 40:09.240
Which one do you want?

40:09.730 --> 40:11.460
The one closest to me.

40:12.920 --> 40:14.170
Thirteen.

40:14.170 --> 40:16.420
Hooray!

40:20.060 --> 40:20.850
Are you okay?

40:21.810 --> 40:23.900
I'm terribly sorry,

40:23.900 --> 40:28.380
but this time I'll give you both my question and dare, so could you choose from them?

40:28.380 --> 40:29.940
Sure, I don't mind.

40:29.940 --> 40:35.360
All right, if you say "truth," you have to tell me three things you find cute about me.

40:36.150 --> 40:39.600
If you say "dare," you have to carry me to bed.

40:42.290 --> 40:45.260
I'll lend you my hand. Come on, stand up.

40:46.960 --> 40:48.790
I can't stand!

40:48.790 --> 40:51.630
My legs are too weak.

40:51.630 --> 40:53.260
That's why I asked you.

40:53.550 --> 40:56.130
Carry me to bed!

41:24.130 --> 41:25.340
Thank you.

41:27.430 --> 41:29.010
Next is the last round.

41:29.010 --> 41:31.090
You should drink some water.

41:33.050 --> 41:34.760
I can't believe that just happened!

41:35.620 --> 41:37.060
Which card do you want?

41:37.860 --> 41:39.130
Let's see...

41:39.130 --> 41:41.670
The one next to my glass.

41:44.020 --> 41:44.800
Seven.

41:46.150 --> 41:47.630
That's iffy!

41:47.630 --> 41:49.680
Iffy, iffy.

41:49.680 --> 41:51.110
Iffy!

41:51.830 --> 41:53.160
What did you get?

41:53.160 --> 41:54.030
Six.

41:54.030 --> 41:55.490
All right!

41:57.780 --> 42:00.070
What should I go with...

42:12.130 --> 42:13.260
Do you want water?

42:37.640 --> 42:39.660
Truth or dare.

42:42.490 --> 42:43.510
Truth.

42:47.180 --> 42:48.000
If I...

42:50.120 --> 42:51.280
If I

42:51.920 --> 42:55.300
told you that I'm actually super scared of dying,

42:55.670 --> 42:57.010
what would you do?

43:31.530 --> 43:32.390
Dare.

43:36.560 --> 43:38.980
Sleep on the bed with me.

43:38.980 --> 43:41.290
No arguing, no debate.

44:07.210 --> 44:07.770
Hello?

44:07.770 --> 44:10.650
Sakura! Where the hell are you?!

44:11.850 --> 44:13.750
Good morning, Kyoko.

44:14.260 --> 44:17.850
You lied to your parents and said you were on a trip with me, right?!

44:17.850 --> 44:21.010
They called us, and it was a real pain to cover for you.

44:21.360 --> 44:23.900
Thanks, Kyoko. Knew I could count on you.

44:23.900 --> 44:28.400
What are you doing sneaking off all alone like you're some dying cat?

44:29.140 --> 44:30.310
I'm not alone.

44:30.310 --> 44:32.020
What? Who's with you?

44:32.020 --> 44:32.950
Your boyfriend?

44:33.800 --> 44:34.900
Don't tell me...

44:34.900 --> 44:36.000
You're with him?

44:36.850 --> 44:41.140
I'll explain all of this to you one day.

44:41.140 --> 44:44.320
So I won't tell you to accept it, but please forgive me.

44:45.860 --> 44:47.550
All right, fine.

44:48.290 --> 44:49.930
But I have conditions!

44:49.930 --> 44:53.980
Come home safe and buy me a souvenir.

44:53.980 --> 44:55.080
And also...

44:55.080 --> 44:57.720
Go on a trip somewhere with me during the summer.

44:59.090 --> 44:59.750
Sure.

44:59.750 --> 45:00.530
Got it.

45:00.530 --> 45:02.090
Also, tell him this.

45:02.550 --> 45:05.470
If he does something to you, he's fucking dead.

45:06.680 --> 45:07.980
I'll let him know.

45:07.980 --> 45:09.160
See you next week.

45:09.160 --> 45:09.720
Yeah.

45:11.450 --> 45:13.640
You might have heard that,

45:13.640 --> 45:16.230
but apparently Kyoko is out to kill you.

45:16.890 --> 45:18.760
That's if I try something, right?

45:18.760 --> 45:21.940
Make sure you tell her I'm innocent.

45:21.940 --> 45:23.920
What about that bridal carry?

45:23.920 --> 45:25.050
Huh...

45:25.050 --> 45:26.940
So that's what it's called.

45:26.940 --> 45:30.290
I was just pretending to be a mover.

45:30.290 --> 45:34.040
If you knew what I was referring to,
you're guilty enough for Kyoko to kill you.

45:43.800 --> 45:46.880
Well, that was over quick.

45:47.850 --> 45:48.480
Yeah.

45:50.250 --> 45:52.450
That jacket suits you.

45:52.450 --> 45:53.890
Don't play games with me.

45:53.890 --> 45:55.050
It's embarrassing.

46:01.050 --> 46:02.920
Well, this is my stop.

46:03.810 --> 46:05.520
We should go on a trip again sometime.

46:06.010 --> 46:07.860
Maybe in the winter next time?

46:10.160 --> 46:11.410
Yeah.

46:11.410 --> 46:12.660
That sounds good.

46:12.660 --> 46:13.680
Oh?

46:13.680 --> 46:15.460
That's awfully honest of you.

46:15.460 --> 46:17.370
Looks like you actually had fun!

46:18.860 --> 46:19.530
Yeah.

46:20.320 --> 46:21.440
It was fun.

46:22.750 --> 46:23.620
What?

46:25.650 --> 46:27.090
What?!

46:35.960 --> 46:37.850
For a few days after I got home,

46:38.310 --> 46:40.430
I spent my days doing nothing in particular.

46:40.940 --> 46:42.360
But then I realized:

46:43.380 --> 46:46.760
I was waiting for her to contact me.

46:48.400 --> 46:52.630
What awaited me as the break ended

46:52.630 --> 46:55.990
was a word of warning from her guardian.

46:57.290 --> 47:00.380
Hey, what were you thinking, going off on a trip like that?

47:02.080 --> 47:05.770
No matter how she might seem,
she gets hurt easier than most.

47:06.220 --> 47:10.640
In junior high she spent the whole night crying after breaking up with her boyfriend.

47:10.640 --> 47:14.430
She was so depressed that I thought she'd never get back on her feet again.

47:14.430 --> 47:17.280
She was the same when her favorite teacher switched jobs,

47:17.280 --> 47:19.020
and when her parents had a huge fight—

47:19.850 --> 47:21.650
Hey, are you listening?!

47:22.060 --> 47:25.940
You know, Sakura is way more delicate than you think.

47:26.430 --> 47:30.200
Someone has to stay by her side and watch over her.

47:30.620 --> 47:32.540
You think you can do that?

47:32.540 --> 47:34.450
What is Sakura to you?

47:41.710 --> 47:43.210
Would you say something?!

47:46.960 --> 47:50.460
Don't get close to her with half-baked feelings.

47:51.800 --> 47:54.560
If you do anything to hurt her...

47:55.670 --> 47:58.020
I will seriously kill you.

48:12.500 --> 48:14.100
You're late!

48:14.100 --> 48:16.370
I already took care of all the work.

48:16.770 --> 48:19.500
I've put back the returned books.

48:19.500 --> 48:20.560
Sorry.

48:20.560 --> 48:22.010
I was talking to someone.

48:24.350 --> 48:27.370
With this kind of weather, we can't hang out outside.

48:29.990 --> 48:31.470
You should come by my place today.

48:34.020 --> 48:34.950
Hey.

48:36.180 --> 48:37.810
Are you listening?

48:38.390 --> 48:39.040
Huh?

48:39.830 --> 48:41.740
Why don't you come to my place today?

48:41.740 --> 48:42.600
No one's home.

48:44.760 --> 48:48.290
No thanks. That's the opposite way from my house.

48:49.100 --> 48:51.110
Come on, don't be like that.

48:52.180 --> 48:55.600
I don't really read books,

48:55.600 --> 48:59.180
but there's one single book I've liked since I was a kid.

49:01.960 --> 49:03.370
Aren't you curious what it is?

49:06.830 --> 49:07.800
A bit.

49:08.460 --> 49:11.790
I think a person's favorite book says a lot about them.

49:13.130 --> 49:13.880
What book?

49:14.220 --> 49:16.200
The Little Prince! Do you know about it?

49:16.770 --> 49:17.940
Saint-Exupéry?

49:17.940 --> 49:18.600
What?

49:18.600 --> 49:20.180
You know it?

49:20.180 --> 49:26.140
And here I was all excited since even you might not know about a foreign book.

49:26.140 --> 49:27.470
All for nothing.

49:28.180 --> 49:31.270
The fact that you don't think The Little Prince is famous

49:31.270 --> 49:34.140
betrays just how uninterested you are in books.

49:34.930 --> 49:36.640
I see...

49:36.640 --> 49:39.330
Sounds like you've read it, then?

49:41.560 --> 49:43.870
No, I actually haven't yet.

49:44.360 --> 49:45.520
Really?!

49:45.520 --> 49:48.300
In that case I'll let you borrow it, so let's go to my place!

49:48.300 --> 49:50.830
It's really good, so I want to hear what you think!

49:50.830 --> 49:51.880
Come on!

49:59.890 --> 50:01.390
See ya later!

50:02.010 --> 50:03.560
Oh, you can get an item there.

50:05.560 --> 50:07.520
Weren't you going to lend me a book?

50:07.520 --> 50:10.520
Now, now, there's no need to hurry.

50:11.630 --> 50:13.240
There we go.

50:14.560 --> 50:15.490
Hey.

50:15.490 --> 50:17.800
I've been wondering for a while.

50:18.270 --> 50:20.220
Don't you want to get a girlfriend?

50:22.080 --> 50:26.000
I don't want to and can't get a girlfriend.
I don't even have friends.

50:26.880 --> 50:29.960
Even if you don't want a girlfriend, you should make friends at least.

50:30.820 --> 50:32.040
If I feel like it.

50:32.930 --> 50:35.260
If you feel like it, huh...

50:41.340 --> 50:42.340
Hey, so...

50:45.770 --> 50:49.740
You'd never want me as your girlfriend no matter what, right?

50:49.740 --> 50:50.320
Huh?

50:53.900 --> 50:55.660
Way to wipe out!

50:56.490 --> 50:58.240
What are you even saying?

51:00.770 --> 51:02.280
I'm just making sure.

51:05.590 --> 51:06.410
No, I wouldn't.

51:06.850 --> 51:07.810
Good to hear.

51:08.550 --> 51:09.670
That's a relief.

51:12.900 --> 51:14.140
Lend me your book.

51:14.840 --> 51:16.060
I'm going home.

51:16.060 --> 51:16.890
What?

51:16.890 --> 51:19.000
There's no need to rush.

51:49.210 --> 51:54.370
Remember my list of things I want to do before dying? This is part of it.

51:57.160 --> 52:02.190
Doing something naughty with someone who's not my boyfriend and who I'm not in love with.

52:04.250 --> 52:05.970
I don't mind if it's with you.

52:07.330 --> 52:09.380
This is a hug.

52:18.670 --> 52:20.610
The naughty part...

52:20.610 --> 52:22.320
is coming up.

52:33.740 --> 52:37.860
Someone has to stay by her side and watch over her.

52:38.600 --> 52:40.290
You think you can do that?

52:53.980 --> 52:55.980
Just kidding!

52:55.980 --> 53:00.140
The mood got all serious because you wouldn't say anything!

53:00.620 --> 53:02.000
Did I make your heart race?

53:02.600 --> 53:03.930
That was embarrassing.

53:03.930 --> 53:06.330
But I'd call that a resounding success.

53:07.160 --> 53:09.330
I'm just joking around with you.

53:09.330 --> 53:10.800
Like I always do.

53:12.040 --> 53:13.400
What are you thinking?

53:25.580 --> 53:27.260
Wait, what's up?

53:27.260 --> 53:29.510
Let me go, it hurts.

53:29.810 --> 53:31.640
Are you playing along with my joke?

53:32.280 --> 53:34.640
That's unusually nice of you!

53:34.640 --> 53:36.650
But you can let go now...

53:39.800 --> 53:41.150
What are you doing?

53:43.810 --> 53:45.660
Give it a rest!

53:46.030 --> 53:49.730
Do you think it's okay to do something like this to a girl?!

53:49.730 --> 53:50.540
Let me go!

53:51.220 --> 53:51.790
Stop!

53:52.370 --> 53:53.870
Stop already!

53:58.250 --> 53:59.170
Stop...

54:29.920 --> 54:30.560
Hey.

54:43.130 --> 54:44.790
You live around here?

54:45.800 --> 54:47.180
No, I don't.

54:47.510 --> 54:49.670
Why are you here?

54:50.560 --> 54:52.060
Is it Sakura?

54:52.380 --> 54:54.700
Answer me. Is it Sakura?!

54:56.210 --> 54:58.650
Why would Sakura be with someone like you?

55:00.700 --> 55:04.730
Our relationship isn't what you think it is.

55:05.650 --> 55:07.400
Tell me what the hell it is, then!

55:07.400 --> 55:10.590
You’re eating together, just the two of you, you went on vacation,

55:10.590 --> 55:12.760
and today you even went to her house!

55:12.760 --> 55:14.950
Everyone's talking about you!

55:16.200 --> 55:17.520
Either way,

55:17.520 --> 55:20.520
we're not in the kind of relationship you and our classmates think.

55:20.520 --> 55:23.730
Yet Sakura is spending her time with you.

55:24.370 --> 55:29.100
Why is she with someone as sullen and antisocial as you?

55:30.510 --> 55:33.170
Wait! We're not done here!

55:36.140 --> 55:37.560
Listen.

55:37.560 --> 55:39.330
Let me clue you in on something.

55:40.180 --> 55:42.290
It might do you some good.

55:42.290 --> 55:45.150
Apparently she doesn't like guys who won't take no for an answer.

55:45.710 --> 55:47.640
I hear her old boyfriend was like that.

55:49.850 --> 55:52.010
Won't take no for an answer?!

55:52.010 --> 55:54.800
What the fuck do you know?!

55:56.960 --> 55:58.390
What...

55:58.390 --> 55:59.410
are you doing?

56:01.580 --> 56:02.690
Sakura!

56:02.690 --> 56:04.040
Good timing.

56:04.040 --> 56:06.120
I was just talking about you with him.

56:06.120 --> 56:06.670
Hey!

56:06.670 --> 56:07.600
Oh no!

56:08.860 --> 56:10.060
Are you okay?

56:10.710 --> 56:12.980
You're... You're bleeding!

56:13.780 --> 56:14.850
Sakura?

56:15.370 --> 56:16.970
What are you doing with someone like him?

56:17.420 --> 56:18.700
"Someone like him"?

56:18.700 --> 56:19.790
What do you mean?

56:19.790 --> 56:22.540
He's been following you around and annoying you,

56:22.540 --> 56:24.370
so I took care of him for you!

56:24.370 --> 56:27.730
Do you think you're better than him or something?

56:27.730 --> 56:29.120
You're awful!

56:29.120 --> 56:31.240
I hate you, Takahiro!

56:31.860 --> 56:35.120
Never do anything to me or the people around me again!

56:37.090 --> 56:37.830
But...

56:38.420 --> 56:39.620
I did it for your sake—

56:39.620 --> 56:40.700
Goodbye!

56:46.450 --> 56:47.680
Are you okay?

56:51.130 --> 56:54.300
So that was your old boyfriend.

57:00.900 --> 57:06.060
A person like me really shouldn't have tried to interact with others.

57:07.570 --> 57:10.190
If I'd kept to myself, no one would have gotten hurt.

57:10.190 --> 57:11.320
That's not true!

57:11.650 --> 57:13.310
Instead of someone like me,

57:13.310 --> 57:16.950
you should be with someone who truly cares for you, like him or Kyoko!

57:22.890 --> 57:24.380
Besides, we two...

57:25.720 --> 57:28.590
just came across each other by chance at the hospital.

57:33.270 --> 57:35.200
That's not true.

57:35.690 --> 57:37.390
It wasn't a coincidence.

57:37.960 --> 57:39.340
Then what was it?

57:40.720 --> 57:44.160
Everyone is where they are because of the choices they've made.

57:45.140 --> 57:48.930
Us being is the same class wasn't a coincidence either,

57:48.930 --> 57:50.900
and it wasn't something like fate.

57:51.540 --> 57:53.840
That's just your interpretation.

57:59.010 --> 58:01.440
In order to write Living with Dying,

58:01.440 --> 58:03.570
I chose that notebook.

58:05.010 --> 58:09.250
You like books, and you got interested and picked it up.

58:10.690 --> 58:11.710
And then...

58:12.380 --> 58:16.410
you accepted my request.

58:17.790 --> 58:20.640
The choices that you've made until now

58:20.640 --> 58:23.000
and the choices I've made until now...

58:24.190 --> 58:28.450
Each and every one of the choices that we've made piled up

58:29.010 --> 58:31.230
and brought us together.

58:35.050 --> 58:38.870
And that's why we're where we are now.

58:46.540 --> 58:49.780
I'm sorry about before.

58:52.890 --> 58:54.370
But I'm...

58:55.140 --> 58:59.310
really happy that you're here now.

59:01.560 --> 59:02.540
So...

59:06.410 --> 59:08.060
For a little longer...

59:09.410 --> 59:11.650
Just a little bit longer...

59:13.660 --> 59:16.650
Will you stay with me?

59:29.680 --> 59:33.920
I don't think there's much that I can do for you.

59:40.750 --> 59:42.300
That's not true.

59:43.550 --> 59:45.810
I'm really sorry about before.

59:50.140 --> 59:53.040
Come back to my place. I'll lend you a change of clothes.

59:58.080 --> 59:58.850
Thank you.

01:00:03.640 --> 01:00:04.680
For what?

01:00:09.170 --> 01:00:11.710
I read books in the order they're placed on the bookshelf,

01:00:09.790 --> 01:00:11.710
The Little Prince

01:00:12.620 --> 01:00:13.780
so it might take a while.

01:00:14.520 --> 01:00:16.750
Just give it back to me in a year.

01:00:17.500 --> 01:00:19.460
Let's get along until I die.

01:00:20.770 --> 01:00:21.410
Yeah.

